{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH our Elohim cut, etc.</b> Now Moses did not explain what this covenant is — whether it is the covenant that Israel undertook to fulfill the Torah of YHWH, as it is written (Exodus 24:8) ״הִנֵּה דַם הַבְּרִית אֲשֶׁר כָּרַת ה׳ עִמָּכֶם עַל כָּל הַדְּבָרִים״, or the covenant that YHWH cut with Israel that He would not exchange them for another nation, as it is written (Exodus 34:10) ״הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי כּוֹרֵת בְּרִית נֶגֶד כָּל עַמְּךָ״ etc. And they of blessed memory explained that He cut a covenant with them regarding זֹאת, that His Shekhinah would not rest upon the nations. And reason determines that it is about this covenant that he speaks, and this is what he alluded to in saying <b>YHWH our Elohim cut with us</b> — meaning, on account of His being our Elohim and not anyone else's, He cut a covenant with us, and to this the phrase ״הַבְּרִית הַזֹּאת״ that he said afterward refers. According to this, the intent of the verse is to praise Israel for the spiritual attainment from YHWH granted to them, and see the verse that follows this one."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:20.331221231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}